## Summary

**`.ui` files** — All 19 forms (src/ + manualtests/) compile clean under uic 6.11.3. No Qt3Support/uic3-era leftovers; custom-widget headers (`searchlineedit.h`, `edittreeview.h`, `squeezelabel.h`, `lineedit.h`) resolve via INCLUDEPATH. Fixed one stale "WebKit-based" string in `aboutdialog.ui`.

**Translations** — Regenerated all 32 `.ts` against the Qt6 sources via `lupdate-pro -locations none` (447 strings, 29 new). Fixes along the way:
- `ast`, `ca`, `es`, `gl`, `pt_PT` `.ts` files had no `language=` attribute — lupdate refused to touch them. Added.
- Qt6 lupdate's language table doesn't know Asturian (`ast`), so `ast.ts` is updated under a temporary `es` tag (same plural rules) and restored to `ast`.
- `webviewsearch.cpp` used `guard->tr()` inside a lambda — unextractable. Switched to `WebViewSearch::tr()`, "Not Found" is back in the catalogs.

**Install rules** — `make install` now also ships `useragents.xml` to PKGDATADIR (UserAgentMenu prefers the installed copy over the bundled qrc resource — distro/admin override) and the 512px icon. `arora.desktop` dropped the deprecated `Application` category, gained `x-scheme-handler/http(s)` MIME types, and went 755→644 (was causing a `strip` failure in the install rule).

**Docs** — man page now says Qt 6 / WebEngine instead of Qt 4.4 / WebKit, and the dead Google Code bugs URL was fixed.

**Verified** — staged `make install` lays down binary + 32 `.qm` + desktop + 5 icons + man.gz + useragents.xml correctly; `desktop-file-validate` clean; clean qmake6+make with 0 warnings; `--quit-after-load` and `--app-smoke` PASS offscreen.

