## What changed

**htmlToXBel** — rewritten engine-free. The Netscape bookmark format is HTML, not XML (unclosed `<DT>`/`<HR>`/`<DD>`, valueless `FOLDED` attributes), so the task's suggested strict `QXmlStreamReader` couldn't actually parse the fixtures; a small forgiving tag scanner drives `QXmlStreamWriter` instead. Entities decode via `QTextDocumentFragment`, URLs get encodeURI-style percent-encoding, and the `FOLDED` attribute on `<H3>` now exports `folded="true"` (dead code in the old `extract.js` DOM walk). `extract.js` + `source.qrc` deleted; `QT += webkit` gone — the tool only needs QtCore+QtGui and runs under `QCoreApplication`.

**cacheinfo** — `QNetworkDiskCache` **does** exist in Qt6 (the task note was stale), so the tool kept its scope: ported to `QStandardPaths::CacheLocation/browser` with matching `Arora/Arora` app scope so it reads the real app-side NAM cache; usage text now states WebEngine's internal Chromium cache is not inspectable this way.

**placesimport** — retargeted at the MIG06 store by including `src.pri` wholesale (as the Qt4 tool did), so imports write through the real `HistoryManager`. Ported to `fromSecsSinceEpoch` for Firefox µs timestamps, `QString` urls, `Qt::endl`; org scope fixed to `Arora/Arora` so `BrowserPaths` hits the real data dir. This required **`src.pri` `$$PWD`-prefixing** all paths (matching every other .pri in the tree) — a safe mechanical change, app rebuild verified.

**Build** — `tools/` re-added to top-level `SUBDIRS` in `arora.pro`.

## Verified

